  "profile": "Pins the first published candidate that contains every CON.07-CON.16 contract as both the previous and the minimum supported descriptor set. Protobuf definitions follow the additive-only rule of the existing window: published members, types, presence, oneofs, enum numbers and RPC shapes are preserved and only additions are accepted. Closed JSON exception schemas reject unknown fields, so a published schema may not change in place while its x-arcforges-schema-version is unchanged; a change needs a retained published version and a reviewed window update. This is an actual published development candidate, not a stable release or a deployed production client.",
  "coverage": "Previous/current and current/minimum offline matrix over the protobuf services of CON.07-CON.11, CON.13 and CON.14 (and the other services in the same closure), plus content pins for the closed JSON schemas of CON.07, CON.10, CON.12, CON.15 and CON.16. Previous and minimum are the same published candidate, so at the pin the matrix compares the candidate with itself; it detects later change and does not show cross-version evolution of these services. The wire exchange is an independent descriptor-driven reference codec, not the generated C#, TypeScript or Kotlin codecs, and no earlier published client assembly or live service contains these contracts."
